skycue superbuild
=================

The superbuild compiles the following third-party projects from their
upstream source tarballs. Each keeps its own license:

  rtl-sdr        GPL-2.0
  SoapySDR       BSL-1.0
  SoapyRTLSDR    MIT
  dump978        BSD-2-Clause / GPL (per file, see the upstream repository)
  readsb         GPL-3.0
  dump1090       GPL-2.0

These programs are built and run as separate processes. None of them is
linked into skycue code.

Web assets installed with skycue
--------------------------------

The skycue web console loads these third-party libraries from its own
installation, with no network access at run time. Each is installed with its
licence file beside it.

Leaflet 1.9.4 (https://leafletjs.com), BSD-2-Clause, installed with its
LICENSE under www/vendor/leaflet/. Copyright (c) 2010-2023, Volodymyr
Agafonkin; Copyright (c) 2010-2011, CloudMade.

Apache ECharts 5.6.0 (https://echarts.apache.org), Apache-2.0, installed under
www/vendor/echarts/ with its LICENSE and NOTICE. Its NOTICE reads: Apache
ECharts, Copyright 2017-2024 The Apache Software Foundation; this product
includes software developed at The Apache Software Foundation
(https://www.apache.org/).

Parts of ECharts are derived from D3 (https://github.com/d3/d3), BSD-3-Clause,
Copyright 2010-2016 Mike Bostock. All rights reserved. The D3-derived files
are src/chart/treemap/treemapLayout.ts, src/chart/tree/layoutHelper.ts,
src/chart/graph/forceHelper.ts and src/util/number.ts in the ECharts sources;
the D3 licence text is installed as www/vendor/echarts/licenses/LICENSE-d3.

Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com) map data is in the public
domain. skycue does not ship it: scripts that build the offline map tiles
(skycue-make-maps) download it on demand.

skycue source and test data
---------------------------

skycue/tests/fixtures/fisb/tg30.978 is a FIS-B test uplink file from
fisb-decode (https://github.com/rand-projects/fisb-decode,
tg/tg-source/generated/tg30.978), Copyright (C) 2020-2021 Michael Barnes,
redistributed under the BSD-2-Clause Plus Patent License; the full licence
text is in skycue/tests/fixtures/fisb/LICENSE.fisb-decode.

skycue/tests/fixtures/raw/stratux-uat-2015.log.gz is a UAT receiver log from
stratux (https://github.com/cyoung/stratux,
test-data/cyoung-09062015-noproblem-stratux-uat.log, gzip-compressed),
Copyright (c) 2015 Christopher Young, redistributed under the BSD-3-Clause
License; the full licence text is in skycue/tests/fixtures/README.md. The
files under skycue/tests/fixtures/raw/ are in the git repository only; the
release source tarball leaves them out.

The FIS-B decoder in skycue/skycued/src/fisb/ follows the field layouts and
product handling of fisb-decode (same copyright and licence as above). It is
an independent C++ implementation written from docs/fisb-reference.md; no
fisb-decode source code is copied into it.

The Mode S CRC and the UAT Reed-Solomon encoder in skycue/skycue-iqgen/ are
written from the published definitions, with the Reed-Solomon parameters
taken from dump978's uat_protocol.h and fec.cc (BSD-2-Clause); no readsb or
libfec code is copied.

